"Kremti" <kremti@gmail.com> writes:
> So, it's been bugging me.
> 
> What happens if I wish for, say, 2 +3 silver daggers?  What's the odds
> of not getting what I want?

For quantity, a 2/3 chance of getting 2, a 1/3 chance of getting 1 (in
general, a (6-n)/6 chance of getting an asked-for n, a n/6 chance of
getting 1; special rules apply to ammo, missiles, rocks, and candles).

For enchantment, it's slightly trickier; there's a base chance of 3/5
(in general, (6-n)/5) of getting +3 and 2/5 (in general, (n-1)/5) of
getting +0, but in the +0 case you _may_ get +3 instead if the
randomly-generated weapon would have had at least that enchantment
anyway. And if you have negative Luck, you'll get -3 instead of +3.

Note that these calculations are entirely independent; neither the
request nor the result of one will have any effect on the result of
the other.

